<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turkmen</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Turkoman</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Turkmen, or Turkoman, are Oghuz <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkic-peoples">Turkic peoples</a> historically associated with pastoral nomadism in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. Turkmen tribal groups contributed to the forces of many states, including the early Ottoman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beyliks</a>, and the Turkmen confederations of the Qara Qoyunlu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> ruled western Iran in the fifteenth century. The Timurid and Safavid empires both had to contend with Turkmen tribal power.</p></div>
